item4.protocol:
Registration S2-R6G (docs/stage2-R6G-prereg.md), committed before any step below. The rule is frozen at (0.8, 4, 31) through SCSam3/ref_snap.decide, and no constant is rescaled. Window: frames 0-20 (21 frames, as in MUVOD). Per-view J&F x100 = mean over objects of the mean over frames 0-20 (eval/eval_jf.py, bound_th 0.008), the same scale as the c_ini reference.

G1:
- New script MVSeed/s2r6g_snap.py. It imports ref_snap.decide, applies the rule only to the 2 non-c_ini annotated cameras, hard-links everything else and writes a MANIFEST with the snapped list.
- Output folders: ...MSdgtFsCs10kG2Rp and ...XW0MSdgtFsRp.
- Score the rule arms -> Data/MVSeg/jf_s2r6g.json.
- Clusters are scenes (mean of the 2 views); objects are the basic set.

G2 and G3:
- The converter writes:
  - Video/cam0/%06d.jpg (JPEG quality 95, since ref_snap reads .jpg);
  - Mask/cam0/000000.png only;
  - MVSeed_gt/cam0/0/<id>.png;
  - a one-camera config with c_ini = 0.
- GT for frames 1-20 goes to a sealed folder outside the run tree.
- Objects: those present in the frame-0 GT with >= 100 px.
- Run each video in its own container under flock: runMVSeg.py --algo MVOpt --xview-window 0 --ref-cam muvod --seeds-from MVSeed_gt --frame0-seed --ref-snap --save-stages. This command was validated on Fencing v4: 168/168 PNGs reproduced both before and after the snap. Base = <out>_stages/stage2, rule arm = <out>.

Step 0, power gate (GT-free; recorded and committed before unsealing):
- From the run MANIFESTs, count snapped object-frames and the clusters with at least one snap.
- G2 and G3 need >= 30 clusters with a snap and >= 300 snaps; G3 also needs |S| >= 30 videos.
- If G2 fails on 16 shards, fetch the other 48 and recount. If it still fails, the result is 'underpowered' and the GT stays sealed.

Then unseal, score and judge with MVSeed/s2r6g_judge.py -> MVSeed/runs/s2r6g/.

Estimands per tier:
- delta = cluster mean of per-view J&F x100 (rule - base);
- g = cluster mean of the per-snap delta J&F x100 over snapped object-frames;
- pi = gate precision = share of snaps whose copy-GT0 J&F >= 0.98;
- 95% CIs by a 10,000-resample cluster bootstrap, seed 0.

Strata, declared now:
- GT_t pixel-identical to GT_0, or not;
- size bins <2k / 2k-10k / 10k-100k / >=100k px;
- G2: unmoved by metadata (max position change < 1e-3 and quaternion change < 1e-3 over t <= 20) vs moved;
- G3: short side >= 1080 vs < 1080.

Design-data reference (c_ini, E8 headline pair):
- delta_ref = +1.094 per view (scene SD 0.99);
- g_ref = +2.00 over scene clusters (SD 1.30, n = 16), or +2.45 per object-frame;
- pi_ref = 91.7% (4,198/4,577);
- snap rate 57.5%;
- per-snap gain +2.53 on GT-identical frames vs +2.22 on non-identical frames (computed from anat2_H/snap2_H).

Optional G2 add-on, only if the S2-R7 code is merged before G2 runs: a third arm with --ref-snap-mem full on the same videos. It measures the self-memory channel on independent data.

