item3.registration:
S2-R7: S2-R6 decisions fed into the c_ini tracker memory (Rm). Commit as docs/stage2-R7-prereg.md before any arm output exists.

1. Question
On frames where the frozen S2-R6 rule snaps, write the frame-0 prompt mask into the c_ini tracker memory as well as into the output PNG. Does MUVOD stage-2 J&F change? One arm, one run, E8 §5 rule.

2. Arms and folders
- Base H = the existing folder SegMaskSam3XW1CGPS4MSdgeoset_rep_xsFsCs10kG2Rs.
  - E14 headline: basic 92.766 / complete 88.086, scored in Data/MVSeg/jf_e14.json, docker sha256:9064e3dc8548…
  - Not rerun. Determinism is checked by G2 and Z5.
- Arm M = SegMaskSam3XW1CGPS4MSdgeoset_rep_xsFsCs10kG2RmRs.
  - Command: the headline command plus --ref-snap-mem (env REFSNAPMEM=1).
  - The suffix Rm goes immediately before Rs; Rs stays last, per the runMVSeg.py convention.
- Declared now as NOT run, and not to be run on MUVOD without a new registration:
  - replay of H's list (sha256 55a68c328219e15c2767c5efa50a93521379df52a0ddfca9c3bbf60220a8a4f6);
  - injection on crop targets;
  - obj_ptr replacement (M2);
  - cond-frame insertion (M3);
  - a pre-encode hook;
  - a shadow (S) arm.
  The reasons for each are in the GO/NO-GO note.

3. Rule (no new constants)
- T = the c_ini crop targets: c_ini objects o with 0 < area(GT_start == o) < 10,000 px (the --crop-small value), using crop_track.is_target. This is the same set CropSmall builds from the given frame-0 prompt. T is empty when the crop pass is off.
- When: in the lockstep write loop, after the c_ini session (r = reference_view_index) has yielded frame t > start and its PNGs are written, and before session r+1 is advanced.
- For which objects: every c_ini object o not in T with a non-empty frame-start PNG m0.
- Decision: snap = ref_snap.decide(m0, mask_t, I_start, I_t) with TAU 0.8, DELTA 4, DILATE 31.
  - mask_t is the mask just written for frame t.
  - I is the grey image Video/<c_ini>/%06d.jpg, read and resized (INTER_AREA) exactly as snap_in_place reads it.
- If it snaps:
  - mf = tracker._encode_new_memory(...) on o's tracker state, using frame t's cached image features, with:
    - pred_masks_high_res = bilinear(bilinear_antialias(m0 -> 288x288) x 20 - 10 -> 1008x1008), align_corners False. This is the route the frame-0 prompt takes.
    - object_score_logits = the stored entry's;
    - is_mask_from_pts = True.
  - non_cond_frame_outputs[t]['maskmem_features'].copy_(mf), in place, keeping the stored dtype and device. It must be in place because the per-object slices share storage.
- Unchanged:
  - in the entry: obj_ptr, maskmem_pos_enc, object_score_logits, iou_score, eff_iou_score, pred_masks;
  - every cond entry, and every other session;
  - the crop pass;
  - --ref-snap. snap_in_place still runs after the crop pass, so the PNG rule is untouched.
- Consequence: for o not in T, the memory decision and the final PNG decision are the same function of the same inputs. So injected = the run's own PNG snap set minus T, exactly.

4. Refusals
The flag is refused with any of: no --ref-snap; --ref-cam other than muvod; --algo other than MVOpt; --xview-mode E / two-pass; more than one GPU; an explicit --out without RmRs.

5. Pre-sweep gates (GT-free)
Smoke outputs go under a scratch --data-root. They are never scored and are deleted afterwards.
- G0: this file is committed.
- G1: the host and container tests pass.
- G2: a flag-off rerun of Blocks and of Fencing has PNG content_digest == H.
- G3, on Dog (0 c_ini crop targets): arm M is byte-identical (content_digest) to the scratch probe s2r6x/mem/probe_mem.py with PROBE_MODE=inject_mem. The injected (t, obj) lists are equal, and there are 0 feature-cache misses.
If a gate fails: fix it and record an erratum here before the sweep.

6. Watch values (GT-free)
All 17 scenes, checked by MVSeed/s2r7_check.py before any scoring. A failure means no verdict: fix, record an erratum, and rerun the failed scenes (all scenes if the code changes).
- Z1:
  - every camera's frame-start PNGs are byte-identical to H;
  - crop_small targets, kept, why and areas are identical, and every crop-kept PNG is byte-identical;
  - T equals H's c_ini crop targets.
- Z2:
  - (a) injected = the arm's own ref_snap.snapped_files minus T, exactly;
  - (b) injected is a subset of H's non-target snaps (3,181). delta depends only on the video and m0, and every delta-pass non-target frame in H was snapped;
  - (c) at frame start+1, injected == H's non-target snaps at start+1. That is 210 in total: AME 18, AMFP 11, Barn 14, Blocks 11, Breakfast 10, CBA 7, Carpark 9, CoffeeMartini 27, Dog 7, Fencing 4, FlameSteak 36, Frog 0, MATF 13, MartialArts 11, Painter 12, PoznanStreet 8, Welder 12;
  - (d) every injected entry existed in non_cond[t] with object_score_logits > 0;
  - (e) 0 cache misses.
- Z3: every snapped c_ini PNG equals its frame-start PNG, and the MANIFEST records the rule (0.8, 4, 31).
- Z4 (cone): r is the c_ini session position and f1 = start+1. The first frame where session r+d's PNG or view_areas differs from H must be:
  - >= f1 for d >= 1;
  - >= f1+1 for d = 0;
  - >= f1+|d| for d <= -1.
  This follows from mode C: v-1 is read at t and v+1 at t-1.
- Z5: Frog (no injections) is byte-identical to H.
- Z6: the docker image id and the demoSCSam3MVOpt source_digest equal H's; argv equals H's plus --ref-snap-mem; the git HEAD is recorded.

7. Adoption (E8 §5)
On unrounded values, by MVSeed/s2r7_judge.py using the e7_judge helpers load / rows / scene_scores / paired, as in e14_judge --stage 2. M is adopted iff all of these hold:
- all 17 scenes are scored, basic and complete;
- Z1-Z6 pass;
- basic Δ(M - H) > 0, and the 95 % scene-bootstrap CI lower bound > 0 (10,000 resamples, Random(0));
- no scene has basic Δ < -1.0;
- complete Δ >= 0.
Otherwise the verdict is 'not adopted: feeding the S2-R6 decisions into memory gives no measurable gain' ('harms' if the CI upper bound < 0), and the headline is unchanged.

8. Stop rule
No other memory variant (replay, crop targets, M2, M3, hook, other encodings) is run on MUVOD without a new registration. That registration must declare itself a second look at the same test set and be judged with a 97.5 % CI.

9. Disclosure if adopted
The headline becomes ...RmRs, and every mention carries:
'Rs is a post-process designed on the test GT (LOSO +0.387; this covers only the PNG snap). Rm feeds the same online decisions into c_ini's tracker memory. It is one pre-registered run on the same 17 scenes with no stage-2 dev set: Δ x [CI]. Its spread to the other cameras is not covered by LOSO.'
The one-pass ...Rs number stays reported next to it.

10. Predictions (not gates)
- P1: injected count in [3,150, 3,181]. 3,181 is a hard upper bound.
- P2: the arm's own Rs count is in [4,560, 4,600], against H's 4,580. Flips can come only from τ on non-targets or from the reverted targets CoffeeMartini 27, FlameSteak 38 and MATF 29.
- P3: relative memory change of injected entries: median 1-4 %, p90 <= 15 %.
- P4: PNG XOR/union vs H <= 1 % per scored camera and scene; median IoU of the changed PNGs >= 0.99; c_ini PNGs change only from start+2.
- P5: basic Δ in [-0.03, +0.04] (80 %), point estimate +0.01.
  - c_ini contribution in [-0.02, +0.03]; other cameras in [-0.01, +0.01];
  - |complete Δ - basic Δ| <= 0.03;
  - worst scene >= -0.2.
- P6: P(adopt) about 0.25. This is because the sign is uncertain, not because of power: a uniformly tiny effect can pass the bootstrap.
- P7: time <= 1.05x H per scene.

11. Known before registration (disclose)
- GT-free probes on Blocks and CoffeeMartini:
  - re-encoding the stored masks reproduces maskmem bit for bit (320/320 and 1000/1000);
  - injection changes memory by a median 2.1 % (p90 11 %);
  - PNG XOR/union 0.03-0.51 %;
  - the cone is as in Z4.
- Bounds that used GT (from existing runs):
  - reachable unsnapped c_ini loss 0.343 (ceiling), realistic +0.01 to +0.04;
  - other cameras about 0.005 or less;
  - non-reference views at |d| = 1 / 2 / >=3 from c_ini: 2 / 6 / 26;
  - switching cross-view memory on and off moved the |d| = 1 pairs by 0.0008.
- In H: 1,399 of 4,580 snaps are on c_ini crop targets (1,249 kept, 150 reverted).

12. Descriptive only (no role in the verdict)
- c_ini vs other-camera contributions, and the other cameras by |d|;
- c_ini frame classes: snapped in both (Δ exactly 0); newly snapped or lost; unsnapped after the first injection; never-injected objects; T objects. Each class is split by copy-GT0 class (static >= 0.98 / near-static / moving);
- PNG XOR/union per camera;
- memory-change statistics;
- time per scene.

item3.implementation:
No edits to SCSam3/demoSCSam3MVOpt or SCSam3/sam3. That keeps the package source_digest equal to H's (Z6).

1) SCSam3/ref_snap.py, torch-free
- Factor out read_grey(video_dir, t, shape, np, cv2) and region(m0, np, cv2). Both snap_in_place and decide() keep calling them, so bytes are unchanged; the test_ref_snap_rule_is_s2r6 pin must still pass.
- Add class OnlineSnap(out_dir, video_dir, cam, start, exclude, np, cv2). On the first t > start it reads the frame-start PNGs from disk and I_start, and precomputes the dilated region per object once. decide_frame(t, {obj: mask_t}) computes |I_t - I_start| once per frame and returns the snapped objs. The result must be identical to decide(); D[reg].mean() is the same reduction.
- Fix the docstring at :11. The pins live in tests/test_pipeline_inprocess.py; tests/test_ref_snap.py does not exist.

2) SCSam3/runMVSeg.py
- Flag --ref-snap-mem (store_true).
- resolve_run:
  - the refusals of §4;
  - when not args.out, out_name += 'Rm' just before the Rs append;
  - with an explicit --out, require 'RmRs';
  - return ref_snap_mem=bool.
- Before the write loop, when on:
  - compute T from Mask/<c_ini>/<start>.png with crop_track.area_and_box / is_target and the run's crop max_px;
  - build OnlineSnap(exclude=T).
- In the loop, after the PNG write for view == ref_index and frame_idx > start: snapped = online.decide_frame(...), then sc.InjectRefMemory(j, frame_idx, [(o, m0[o]) for o in snapped]).
- New method MVSegVideo.InjectRefMemory, following probe_mem.py:
  - state = predictor._ALL_INFERENCE_STATES[session_ids[j]]['state'];
  - ts = model._get_tracker_inference_states_by_obj_ids(state, [o])[0];
  - e = ts['output_dict']['non_cond_frame_outputs'][t]; a missing entry is recorded as an error;
  - record the cache hit before _get_image_feature(ts, t, 1);
  - inside torch.inference_mode(): the encode of §3, then e['maskmem_features'].copy_(mf.to(stored dtype, device));
  - record rel = |mf - old| / |old|.
- After CropSmall: sys.exit if T != the c_ini targets in crop_stats.
- MANIFEST provenance 'ref_snap_mem': null when off, else {rule, encoding, T, injected ['cam/t/obj.png'], n_injected, n_decided, missing_entries, cache_misses, rel_change {median, p90, max}, seconds}.

3) SCSam3/runMVOptThree.sh
Add ${REFSNAPMEM:+--ref-snap-mem} and a usage line.

4) Tests
- tests/test_pipeline_inprocess.py, host:
  - out_name ...Cs10kG2RmRs;
  - each refusal;
  - flag-off resolve_run equals the previous dict plus ref_snap_mem False;
  - OnlineSnap.decide_frame gives the same snapped set as snap_in_place on a synthetic folder, with exclusion;
  - T equals select_targets_from's c_ini targets on synthetic GT.
- Container test (torch + sam3, tests/harness bare tracker if feasible): InjectRefMemory writes in place and is visible through output_dict_per_obj; obj_ptr, scores and cond entries are unchanged.

5) MVSeed/s2r7_check.py
Computes Z1-Z6 from MANIFESTs and PNGs (GT-free) -> MVSeed/runs/s2r7_check.json.

6) MVSeed/s2r7_judge.py
E7.load(['jf_s2r7.json', 'jf_e14.json']), rows basic and complete, scene_scores, paired, DEFENCE -1.0, plus the descriptives -> MVSeed/runs/s2r7_judge.json.

Byte-identity when off: no new code path executes and resolve_run's out_name is unchanged. MANIFEST gains only 'ref_snap_mem': null, and content_digest excludes MANIFEST. G2 verifies Blocks and Fencing against H.

